# JarvOS continuity — unit capture rules.
#
# `jarvos-sync` captures enabled units in both scopes, subtracts the ones the
# distro already enables (system/services/enable.txt), then drops anything
# matching a pattern here. What survives is genuinely the user's: their
# watchers, timers, agents and daemons.
#
# Patterns are bash globs matched against the unit name. One per line.

# Instantiated / device- and mount-bound units: meaningless on another box.
*@*.service
*@*.timer
*.mount
*.automount
*.swap
*.device
*.scope
*.slice

# Shipped and enabled by the OS itself; re-enabling them is noise at best.
systemd-*
dbus-*
getty*
console-getty*
autovt*
remote-fs*
ldconfig*
man-db*
shadow*
archlinux-keyring-wkd-sync*
systemd-tmpfiles-*
plymouth*

# Unit generated by the JarvOS installer per machine.
jarvos-monitor-layout.*

# Anything the display manager owns — chosen at install, not carried over.
sddm*
gdm*
lightdm*
